I happen to be the current director

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.240
of the Franke Program in
Science and Humanities.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.831
I'm delighted to see you all here

00:00:18.831 --> 00:00:21.780
for the Franke Distinguished
Speaker Series,

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.710
in which we have featured leading thinkers

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.741
whose work and intellectual influence

00:00:25.741 --> 00:00:29.470
transcends traditional
disciplinary boundaries.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.960
First I would like to
thank our generous donors,

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.310
Mr. and Mrs. Richard
Franke, Richard and Barbara,

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:36.740
who are here in the audience.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.740
Thank you so much for not
just endowing this series,

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:47.650
but also being here with us
and participating actively

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.750
in the activities that
we've been organizing.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.640
So, second, after the
talk I want to mention

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.172
we have a very nice reception
downstairs in room 108,

00:00:58.172 --> 00:01:01.750
and I wanted to remind you
that we would really like

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.383
